---
// stead.ing's front page: where software is going and how to start today,
// then which project fixes your problem, how they fit together, that it's
// real, and how to build it with us. The hero's words come from
// content/site.yaml.
import type { Landing } from "../lib/schema.ts";
import { SITE } from "../site.ts";
import FlowMap from "./motifs/FlowMap.astro";
import Timeline from "./motifs/Timeline.astro";
import ProjectIndex from "./ProjectIndex.astro";
import PromptBox from "./PromptBox.astro";

interface Props {
  landing: Landing;
}

const { landing } = Astro.props;
const sentences = landing.headline.split(/(?<=\.)\s+/);
---

<section class="hero wrap">
  <h1 class="display">{sentences.map((sentence) => <span>{sentence} </span>)}</h1>
  <p class="lead measure">{landing.summary}</p>
  <PromptBox prompt={landing.prompt} />
  <p class="facts">
    Paste the prompt into your agent, or <a href="#projects">start with the project for your problem</a>.
  </p>
  <Timeline id="hero" view={{ pxPerHour: 130, backlog: false, threads: true, speed: 1 / 10, tone: "muted", compact: true }} />
</section>

<section class="band band-surface" aria-labelledby="why">
  <div class="wrap why">
    <div>
      <h2 id="why" class="display-2">You've got more ideas than hours.</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 measure">
        You pay for a model subscription (or <em>four</em>) and either max it out or barely use it. Not for lack of ideas, but
        because babysitting agents eats up most of your time.
      </p>
      <!-- Each step leads to the next, a little further off course. -->
      <ol class="drift">
        <li>Talk out a problem.</li>
        <li>Set a goal.</li>
        <li>Switch windows.</li>
        <li>Lose the thread.</li>
        <li>Find out your agent is blocked.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="monday"><em>Every morning feels like Monday brain.</em></p>
    </div>
    <div class="pullout measure">
      <p>
        So you try to build a software factory. Everyone does eventually. Then every tool becomes one more thing to patch,
        deploy, sandbox, and secure, and you spend more time building the factory than you would have building your original
        idea.
      </p>
      <p>
        Steading's goal is to reclaim your time and let you direct a <em>fleet</em> rather than babysit a <em>swarm</em>. You
        hash out the plan with an agent, and it builds, prioritizes, and decomposes a backlog for maximum parallelism, with as
        many resources as you feel like throwing at it.
      </p>
      <p>
        You're free to play a video game or watch a show. The agents will let you know if they need anything. You come back
        to merged, running changes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Steading is the loop, with the fences, the upkeep, and the proof already built in. It's how Steading builds itself
        today, and it's yours to run tonight!
      </p>
      <PromptBox prompt={landing.prompt} id="prompt-why" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="projects">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="projects" class="display-2">What's your biggest bottleneck?</h2>
    <p class="lead measure mt-4">
      Start with what's slowing you down today. Every project works on its own, and they get better <em>together</em>.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10">
      <ProjectIndex />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-surface" aria-labelledby="idea">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="idea" class="display-2">A platform you can take apart</h2>
    <p class="subtitle">Great on its own, better together</p>
    <p class="lead measure mt-4">
      Everyone else is building one big system for you to move into. Steading is a platform too, but it's made of projects,
      each built to do one job well, each with an open interface. If you have a better idea for a project, swap in your own;
      the rest keeps working.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10">
      <FlowMap id="map" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-surface" aria-labelledby="beliefs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="beliefs" class="display-2">What we believe</h2>
    <dl class="beliefs mt-10">
      <div>
        <dt>You decide what. Agents do the rest.</dt>
        <dd>Nobody should have to sit in a chat window for work to move.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Proof, not promises.</dt>
        <dd>"Done" means a program checked it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Real fences, not polite requests.</dt>
        <dd>
          What an agent can touch is limited by the operating system, the network, or a virtual machine, not by a sentence in a
          prompt.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Code over prompts.</dt>
        <dd>A model is called only where judgment is actually needed.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Yours.</dt>
        <dd>Your hardware, your database, your rules.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Fork it.</dt>
        <dd>Take any project and make it your own. Send back what's worth sharing.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="join">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="join" class="display">Don't build it all on your own!</h2>
    <p class="lead measure mt-6">
      Everyone is building their own version of this and hitting the same walls. Build it with a community instead. Come
      hang out on <a href={SITE.chat}>Discord</a>, pick up an open task, ask questions, or show us what you've made!
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-2">
      <a href={SITE.chat}>Join the Discord</a>
      <a href="/how-we-work/">How we work, and how a project joins</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/steading-ai">Steading on GitHub</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }
  /* A grid item is as wide as its widest content unless told otherwise. The day strip is another component's element, so the rule has to reach past this one's own. */
  .hero > :global(*) {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .display span {
    display: block;
  }
  /* The first step is the point of the page: it takes the full width, at a size that says so. */
  .hero :global(.prompt) {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .hero :global(.prompt pre) {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .facts {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .hero :global(.timeline) {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 72rem) {
    /* The headline on one line across the page. */
    .display span {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  .why {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .why {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 4rem;
    }
  }
  .subtitle {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  /* Each step hangs off the one before by an arrow, and sits a little further off course. */
  .drift {
    --indent: 1.6rem;
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 3.2vw, 1.35rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .drift li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: calc(var(--step) * var(--indent));
  }
  .drift li + li {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    padding-left: calc((var(--step) - 1) * var(--indent) + 2.1rem);
  }
  .drift li:nth-child(1) {
    --step: 0;
  }
  .drift li:nth-child(2) {
    --step: 1;
  }
  .drift li:nth-child(3) {
    --step: 2;
  }
  .drift li:nth-child(4) {
    --step: 3;
  }
  .drift li:nth-child(5) {
    --step: 4;
  }
  /* The arrow's stem and shaft: down from under the step before, then across. */
  .drift li + li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: calc((var(--step) - 1) * var(--indent) + 0.45rem);
    top: -0.7rem;
    width: 1rem;
    height: 1.35rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--muted);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--muted);
  }
  /* And its head. */
  .drift li + li::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: calc((var(--step) - 1) * var(--indent) + 1.35rem);
    top: 0.33rem;
    border-block: 0.3rem solid transparent;
    border-left: 0.45rem solid var(--muted);
  }
  .monday {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* The turn in the story, set apart from what led to it. */
  .pullout {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--ember);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .pullout :global(figure) {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .beliefs {
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .beliefs > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem 3rem;
    padding-block: 1.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .beliefs dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .beliefs > div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    }
  }
</style>
